- trueqbit: the header opens with `Purpose:`; the file's path and name
  carry its brief description, and what the name leaves unsaid goes into
  the Purpose's first clause. A summary line before the labels, as the
  Cashbook repository has, is left out: there the header is the JSDoc of
  the exported class and an editor shows its first line on hover, while an
  `@file` block attaches to no declaration. The amalgamation keeps the name
  beside each block through its `// #include "..."` line.

